    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12438817/comment/12768727",
          "id": "12768727",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "glen, I know there is an oracle domain index implementation too, so maybe a database category isn't a bad idea.\n\ndo you know of any others?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-10-22T15:41:26.827+0000",
          "updated": "2009-10-22T15:41:26.827+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12438817/comment/12768743",
          "id": "12768743",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=gnewton",
            "name": "gnewton",
            "key": "gnewton",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Glen Newton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "[DBSight|http://www.dbsight.net/] is a commercial product that does indexing and a lot more.\n\nI was wondering if there is the need for another category: Other projects/frameworks that have support for or are built on, Lucene internally (as opposed to \"Lucene Tools\". Examples:\n* [Compass|http://www.compass-project.org/]\n* [Hibernate|https://www.hibernate.org/410.html]\n* [SOLR|http://lucene.apache.org/solr/]\n* others...???\n\nIn the FAQ, for [http://wiki.apache.org/lucene-java/LuceneFAQ#How_can_I_use_Lucene_to_index_a_database.3F|indexing databases with Lucene], LuSql should also be added (separate JIRA issue?)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=gnewton",
            "name": "gnewton",
            "key": "gnewton",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Glen Newton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-10-22T16:24:39.793+0000",
          "updated": "2009-10-22T16:24:39.793+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12438817/comment/12768745",
          "id": "12768745",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Glen, I think it would  be good to bring the contributions page completely up to speed.\n\nmaybe for this issue, we stick with database integration though for simplicity? :)\n\nbq. In the FAQ, for [http://wiki.apache.org/lucene-java/LuceneFAQ#How_can_I_use_Lucene_to_index_a_database.3F|indexing databases with Lucene], LuSql should also be added (separate JIRA issue?)\n\nI think you can just register to the wiki and edit this yourself?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
